  "notes": "Fewer than 100 per sex because the source is thresholded: only names with >1,000 entries within a single municipality appear (min value in file is 1,001). The file has 1,723 rows (202 municipalities, gender field ΑΡΡΕΝ=male, ΘΗΛΥ=female, columns regionalUnitName, municipalityName, firstName, gender, recordCount); it yields 52 male and 59 female distinct names, so these lists are complete for what the source publishes, not truncated by us. Source publishes no rank; ranks are ours, by descending summed count (ties by name). Because a name is dropped in any municipality where it has 1,000 or fewer entries, the summed counts undercount, and undercount small/regional names most; ranks in the lower part of each list (below about the 20th) are approximate. Names are the official registry forms (e.g. Γεώργιος, Ιωάννης, Δημήτριος), not colloquial forms (Γιώργος, Γιάννης, Δημήτρης); the source also contains accent-less (tonos-missing) register spellings as SEPARATE rows (data-entry variants of the same name); we kept every source row unmerged, with source spelling. Male variants (accentless row -> accented row): Γεωργιος->Γεώργιος, Κωνσταντινος->Κωνσταντίνος, Ιωαννης->Ιωάννης, Δημητριος->Δημήτριος, Νικολαος->Νικόλαος, Παναγιωτης->Παναγιώτης, Χρηστος->Χρήστος, Βασιλειος->Βασίλειος, Εμμανουηλ->Εμμανουήλ, Μιχαηλ->Μιχαήλ, Ευαγγελος->Ευάγγελος, Αντωνιος->Αντώνιος, Αγγελος->Άγγελος. Female: Μαρια->Μαρία, Ελενη->Ελένη, Αικατερινη->Αικατερίνη, Βασιλικη->Βασιλική, Σοφια->Σοφία, Αναστασια->Αναστασία, Ειρηνη->Ειρήνη, Ευαγγελια->Ευαγγελία, Αγγελικη->Αγγελική, Αννα->Άννα, Ολγα->Όλγα (here Ολγα is the accentless row and Όλγα the accented one). After merging these, 39 male and 48 female distinct names remain; reviewers should merge by accent-stripped form and use the accented spelling. Measures people on the active register of all ages, so it reflects names of older generations, not recent newborn trends. Earlier snapshots 22/07, 19/08, 01/09 (two resources) 2026 give near-identical totals (112-114 distinct names). ELSTAT (statistics.gr) was checked: it published only percentage shares of the top 20-30 names per birth year 1940-2021 as videos/infographics, no downloadable count table for 100 names, so it was not used. Cyprus fallback was not needed.",
  "source_id": "src_name_frequency_el_gr_data_gov_gr_ypes"
